    <string name="privacy_who_title">Who we are</string>
    <string name="privacy_who">This app is made by wander wildwood, an independent developer: one person, not a company. That makes wander wildwood the data controller for anything the app itself handles, and that is very little: what you put in stays on this phone. The only things that go out are the requests described above: to the sites, podcasts and capsules you add, one for each feed, page, episode or capsule, carrying its address and the app\'s name and version; and, only if you sign in to one, to your feed server, carrying your login, your feeds\' addresses and folders, and what you have read or starred. Nothing comes to the developer.</string>
    <string name="privacy_contact_title">How to contact us</string>
    <string name="privacy_contact">Write to email@wanderthe.dev, about your data or anything else.</string>
    <string name="privacy_rights_title">Your rights</string>
    <string name="privacy_rights">Under the GDPR you can ask to see the data held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to limit or object to its use, to take a copy with you, to withdraw consent, and to complain to a data protection authority. Since the app keeps what it stores only on your phone, you can do most of this yourself: export your feeds as OPML, remove a feed or a page you kept, forget a capsule\'s certificate in Settings, stop syncing to forget a feed server\'s address and login, clear the app\'s data in Android\'s settings, or uninstall the app. What the sites, podcasts and capsules you add, and a feed server you sign in to, receive is covered by their own privacy policies. A server of your own is yours: what it keeps is up to you.</string>
